  "provenance": {
    "base": "instruction.md 6.2: constructed from domain knowledge in the same style as 6.1",
    "additions": [],
    "reason": "The German SCM has no literal specification in the instruction; it follows the loan-application semantics documented in german.doc and the same reference papers."
  },
  "notes": [
    "installment_rate is the instalment as a band of disposable income and is therefore mechanically determined by credit_amount and duration: any method that changes the loan terms without re-deriving it produces a causally impossible profile. This is the central causal-validity test case for this dataset.",
    "purpose, credit_amount and duration are application-form variables: an applicant can genuinely change them at zero real-world cost by asking for a different loan, which makes them the cheapest legitimate recourse levers.",
    "credit_history is a factual record of the past, so it is non-manipulable even though it is not a protected attribute.",
    "age -> credit_risk and sex -> credit_risk are drawn because German scorecards do use them; keeping the edges lets the fairness analysis measure the direct effect instead of hiding it.",
    "credit_risk is a sink."
  ]
